    "description": "API - SF-508 - Opportunity 'Win Reason' Validation Rules Update\n\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nGenerated: 2026-01-14\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nSUMMARY:\n  Opportunity 'Win Reason' Validation Rules Update\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n  As an MRD I want to define a win reason for an opportunity that is not listed \n  in the picklist values. When I specify that the win reason is 'Other', I must \n  be forced to input a value in the Win reason details field before I can save \n  the record.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n  1. When Win Reason is set to 'Other', Win_reason_details__c field must be populated\n  2. Validation rule enforces mandatory Win_reason_details__c when Win Reason = 'Other'\n  3. Field exists on Opportunity object\n\nAPI TESTING REQUIREMENTS:\n  - Verify Win_reason_details__c field exists on Opportunity\n  - Create Opportunity with Win reason details\n  - Update Win_reason_details__c on Opportunity\n  - Query Opportunity by Win reason details\n  - Negative/boundary scenarios (invalid values, null handling)\n\nGenerated from: src/features/api/SF/SF-508.feature\n\nThis collection contains API tests for SF-508 work item.",
